# Plated — environment config.
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is gitignored — never commit keys.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars are bundled into the app at build time.

# Supabase (Project Settings → API)
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY

# Foursquare Places (foursquare.com/developers → your project → Service Key).
# NOT an app env var at all — it lives as a Supabase Edge Function secret, because
# it is billable and anything EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed ends up readable in the bundle:
#
#   supabase secrets set FOURSQUARE_KEY=your-service-key
#
# The client reaches Foursquare only through the `places` function, which requires
# a signed-in user. Nothing here.

# Google Maps SDK (console.cloud.google.com → enable "Maps SDK for iOS" /
# "Maps SDK for Android" → Credentials → create + restrict a key per platform).
# NOT EXPO_PUBLIC_-prefixed: read by app.config.ts at prebuild time only, baked
# into native Info.plist/AndroidManifest.xml — never bundled into the JS app.
GOOGLE_MAPS_IOS_API_KEY=YOUR-IOS-MAPS-API-KEY
GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY=YOUR-ANDROID-MAPS-API-KEY

# Directions is NOT an app env var either — it's an Edge Function secret:
#
#   supabase secrets set GOOGLE_DIRECTIONS_KEY=your-directions-key
#
# Use a SEPARATE key from the two above, restricted to the Directions API. It
# can't share the Maps SDK key: bundle-id restrictions only apply to client
# SDKs, while Directions is a web service API that accepts IP restrictions only
# — unusable from a phone. So the SDK key must stay bundle-id-restricted (it
# ships in Info.plist) and the Directions key must stay server-side. One key
# cannot satisfy both. See DEPLOYMENT.md §8.
